# Build context for infrastructure/docker/Dockerfile.
#
# The Dockerfile runs `COPY . .`, so anything not excluded here ends up both in
# the context sent to the daemon and in a layer of the `build` stage. Two
# classes of file must never get there: secrets, and host-built state that the
# image is supposed to produce for itself.

# --- Secrets: never in a build context, never in a layer -------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
secrets/

# --- Host dependency trees and build outputs -------------------------------
# The image installs from the lockfile and compiles from source. A host
# node_modules carries Windows/macOS native binaries (argon2, Prisma engines)
# that do not run on Alpine.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/coverage
**/.turbo
# Must go with dist: `tsc -b` trusts a tsbuildinfo, so copying one without its
# dist makes the compiler decide everything is up to date and emit nothing.
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/next-env.d.ts

# --- Local data -------------------------------------------------------------
.pgdata/
logs/
**/*.log

# --- Test artefacts and load-test output (fixture.json holds credentials) --
apps/api/loadtest/fixture.json
apps/api/loadtest/results/
apps/web/test-results/
apps/web/playwright-report/
apps/web/blob-report/
apps/web/playwright/.cache/
apps/web/e2e/.auth/

# --- VCS, editor and agent state -------------------------------------------
.git/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
